prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids has come in under 90% of normal in September to October 38 times in 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025, on the middle of the grids, October to November came in at 42% and November to December at 55%. So far in 2026, March to April sits at 43% and April to May at 60% on the middle of the grids. Grids 20606 and 20607 had their driest year in 1963 at 61%.</p>"}
